@startuml
' Authored fixture (svg-sprite-nanoparser, 2026-07-30).
' Sprites come from the stdlib bundle via !include -- the form a user
' actually writes (si8 T6). This fixture previously inlined the `sprite
' <name> <svg ...>` declarations because the golden harness (renderFixture)
' ran the preprocessor with NO include resolver; si8 T5 wired one in, so
' that workaround is gone.
' The MULTI-LINE case, which is the actual defect. A single-line sprite
' display is already correct (only the ellipse consumes the dimension); with
' two or more lines the stacking cursor advances by whatever the atom
' reports, so an ink-valued dimension makes line 2 stack short. This is the
' 0.029321in widening on bootstrap-0 / ruziru-69-xixo434.
skinparam UsecaseBackgroundColor white

!include <bootstrap/bootstrap>

usecase a as "<$bi-globe>\nbi-globe"
usecase b as "<$bi-bootstrap-fill,scale=2.5>\nline two\nline three"
usecase c as "text first\n<$bi-globe,scale=2.5>"
@enduml
